  "caption": "Quinn's big netball moment: fake left, go right… and the kneecap went left anyway, then slid back as the leg straightened.\n\nA kneecap that slips sideways is most common in teens and young adults. After a first episode, the main goal is lowering the chance of another one, and strength and control are big levers.\n\nRehab often includes quad strength, hip strength to stop the knee caving in, and landing, balance and change-of-direction practice. Finishing rehab matters: return to sport often takes three to six months.\n\nIf the kneecap slips, the knee swells quickly, locks or keeps giving way, get it checked by a doctor.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
